WEBVTT

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.700
Hi, this is Dr. Jelena Trajkovic with CECS Department at Cal State Long Beach. So, how does it work?

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:18.700
Okay, let's look at it. Where do we start? We have to start with initial state or start state.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:31.950
And maybe I should actually look, wait for me to write something before I start talking way too much.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:45.280
So, start with initial state and based on the state transition diagram we know that

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:54.220
it is state S0 that we start with and we are in start at 0 we are generating or actually

00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:14.190
FSM is generates output corresponding output which in this case happens to be 0.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:30.990
we are sitting and waiting for a value of input. Depending on the input value, we are

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:49.020
going to transition in the next state. So, if input value input is equal to zero, we

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:56.500
are going to basically stay in the same state and produce the same output. If input value

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:07.040
becomes 1, we are going to go into state 1 and produce output 1. When we come to the

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:14.320
following state, irrespective of which one it is, we are going to stay in that state

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:22.160
and wait for the input. So, transition is always based on the value of the input.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:44.030
Addition thing that I wanted to show you is what is happening in state S1.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:51.750
When we reach the state S1, and we need to look at the state transition diagram at the

00:02:51.750 --> 00:03:04.280
top of this page, irrespective if we get input 0 or input 1, we are going to go to S0.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:19.080
So basically on input equal to 0 and on input equal to 1, transition to S0 and change the

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:26.360
value of the output to 0.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:35.100
Now a couple of things also to mention.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:51.780
So many times, what is not said, but assumed, is that there will be a clock running.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:58.840
And we will be, on each positive edge of the clock, going to basically sample the value

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.720
of input, check the value of the input, and on that positive edge of the clock, based

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:09.160
on the input, we are going to transition somewhere, in one of the other states.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:16.340
So that is another assumption that we can make.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:20.020
Not all FSM work that way.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:25.020
Some FSM are going to have only input

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:30.340
and no clock and that is a possibility.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.100
The other thing that I wanted to show you

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:39.440
is when you look at the FSM here,

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:54.290
We will be in state as 0 and that state as 0 is going to make the output, so this is

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:57.660
state.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:06.020
So we are in state as 0, let's go to timing diagrams and that one is going to generate

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:11.490
an output of 0.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:22.550
If the input is 1, we will go to state S1 and we will have 1.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:30.830
Now regardless of what is next input, so this is, I am doing this impromptu just to let

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:42.670
you know and so if we are in S0 and input became 1, we are transitioning to S1 and irrespective

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:46.790
if the input stays one or if it changes to zero,

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:57.340
we will be going back to S zero.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.000
And then we will stay in S zero

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.000
as long as we have on the input value zero.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:10.700
So what this FSM is doing is generating a short pulse

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.240
that is equal to one every time that we find

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.050
that the input is one.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.050
Thanks for watching.

